  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Blustery and much turning much colder tonight \nand Saturday\n\nThe post-frontal winds gusting 25-35 mph direct much colder air\ninto CPA through tonight into Saturday. Clouds and winds have\nresulted in slightly warmer overnight low temps so advective\nfreeze is probably off the table for the NW mtns. Low level flow\nturns more northerly overnight which should limit lake effect\nresponse, although a few rain/snow showers remain possible over\nthe higher terrain. Min wind chills by Saturday morning will be\nin the 25-35F range across the western and central Alleghenies.\nHighs on Saturday will be 20 to 30 degrees colder vs. Friday. \n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Frost and freeze conditions Saturday night into \nearly Sunday\n\nFrost/freeze still looks good for Saturday night into early\nSunday morning as clouds fade and winds subside. Issued Freeze\nwatch for active zones in the late innings of the growing\nseason.",
